  "enL": "Tian Xing imagery: first, law and rules—Tian Xing in Life Palace means principled, rule-abiding, suitable for law, enforcement, auditing, compliance. Second, litigation and disputes—Tian Xing in Career or Friends Palace, work easily involves contract disputes, personnel conflicts. Third, surgery and injury—Tian Xing in Health Palace, watch for diseases requiring surgery (tendency, not certainty). Fourth, solitary harshness—heavy Tian Xing people have cold personalities, poor at expressing emotions, easily give others a sense of distance in relationships. Tian Yao imagery: first, charm and romance—Tian Yao in Life or Migration Palace, has opposite-sex appeal, good at socializing, attractive appearance. Second, talent and aesthetics—Tian Yao governs artistic sensitivity, suitable for design, beauty, entertainment, PR industries requiring美感. Third, allure and ambiguity—Tian Yao in Spouse or Fortune Palace, relationships prone to ambiguity or polygamous tendencies, need to watch boundaries. Usage principle: they are \"adjectives\" not \"subjects.\" To judge a palace fortune, first look at major stars and transformations, then Tian Xing/Tian Yao as modifiers. For example, Life Palace Zi Wei (strong major star) + Tian Xing (adds principled) = suitable for management and legal affairs; Life Palace Tan Lang (romantic major star) + Tian Yao (adds charm) = talent for social and entertainment industries. If Tian Xing and Tian Yao both appear in Spouse Palace, it may be a partner with both charm and principle, or \"relationships involving legal issues\" (such as marital property disputes), requiring综合 judgment with transformations.",
